  "_comment": "Claude Code model config for the orca app. Seeded into /home/orca/.claude/settings.json by entrypoint.sh as a GAP-FILL merge: the on-disk file wins for existing keys, so a key already on the orca-home volume is never overwritten. jq '*' deep-merges OBJECTS but REPLACES arrays, so: a scalar/array key that exists on disk is protected, but a NEW key inside an existing object (e.g. a new key in 'env') IS added. This file only takes effect on a FRESH volume; the live volume keeps its own array. Mirrors the live volume file exactly as of 2026-10-08 (23 picker rows). Edit the volume file for runtime changes; edit this file only to change what a fresh volume gets. NOTE: each ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL_NAME must equal its ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL, or the picker shows one name and runs another model.",
